# The software stack for every Frontier build and run: one `module load` of these lines, in order.
# Pinned from the Phase 7 login-node probe (meta repo knowledge/frontier/probe-2026-11-25.txt) to
# match Tuolumne where Frontier has it: ROCm 7.14 (7.14.1 here) and Cray MPICH 9.1.0.
# cce stays at cpe/26.03's default (21.0.4): OLCF's metis and darshan-runtime modules live under
# it, and any other cce makes Lmod refuse the whole load. The compilers are ROCm's amdclang (see
# frontier.sh); cce only picks the module hierarchy.
# Changing a line changes the stack: change SD_STACK_TAG in frontier.sh with it.
libfabric/2.3.1
PrgEnv-cray/8.7.0
cpe/26.03
cce/21.0.4
cray-mpich/9.1.0
rocm/7.14.1
craype-accel-amd-gfx90a
metis/5.1.0
